  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What changed\n- `painted::cell`: the label shrinks 13 -> 10 px to fit its cell; only a label still too wide at 10 px elides.\n- The four section doors read \"Mill 2D...\", \"Mill 3D...\", \"Drill...\", \"Multi...\" (full name stays in the tip and dropdown), so they are no longer three identical \"Milli...\" buttons.\n- Group captions are painted again (`painted::caption`, replacing `let _ = captions;`), under the cells, when they fit the group's span: File, Setup, Modify, Inspect, View. Single-door groups skip it (the cell already names the section; four wide adjacent captions would collide). Recorded in `docs/decisions/948-ribbon-labels.md`.\n- `interact::ground_grid_lines`: returns no lines for a non-finite or >1e9 camera target/step (dist 1e308 overflowed `reach` and the loop walked all of i64).\n\n## Tests\n- `structural::ribbon_labels_whole_and_captions_painted` (ui lib): at 1280 px no ribbon galley is elided, each of 24 button labels is painted exactly once (no duplicate text), the five captions are painted under the cells, left to right.\n- `law_tests::the_ground_grid_survives_a_nan_or_huge_camera` (NaN, inf, 1e308 cases).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (ui lib + boundary, boundary_picks, edge_loop_pick, operations, theme_files); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nPNG goldens are left unchanged for the cut (they will differ: labels and captions). No visual check of a real GPU window.\n\nChangelog: Ribbon buttons read whole at 1280 px (short door labels, labels shrink to fit) and the group captions are back; a non-finite camera no longer hangs the ground grid (#948, PR #970)\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #948",
